A||||13||Cheever2||Who loves JAZZ?  Who do you like?||||6||
Z||000000||Cheever2||10-29-2000||03:08 AM||||I can't get enough jazz music.  <BR>I mostly like contemporary "smooth" jazz.  Did a search here and didn't find much discussion about it, but I know you cool cats are out there.  <BR>Groups I like are The Rippingtons, Yellow Jackets, Spyro Gyra, Pieces of a Dream.  <BR>On keyboard I like Bob James, Ramsey Lewis, Dave Grusin, Keiko Matsui, Joe Sample.<BR>Guitar: Lee Ritenour, Evan Marks, George Benson, Craig Chaquicuo.  <BR>Sax: Gato Barbieri, Grover Washington Jr.<BR>Trumpet: Rick Braun, Wynton Marsalis.  Vocals: Cassandra Wilson, Sade.<BR>Flute: Jerauld Dameon, Tim Weisburg.<P>And I'm just getting started!  Dim the lights, put something nice on, and tell ol' Cheever2 who it is you like to listen to when you want that special mood.  Yeah.  Mmm.  Alright.<P><BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Phil||10-29-2000||07:23 AM||||Everytime I find a "smooth jazz" station on the radio they change formats after a few months --very annoying||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||10-29-2000||08:46 AM||||Next time you're buying music, buy "Turning Night into Day" by Nelson Rangell. It will become one of your all time favorites.<P>Smooth jazz lovers basically must have Internet Audio...it seems like the stations don't survive very long.<P>Try <A HREF="http://www.BroadcastAmerica.com" TARGET=_blank>www.BroadcastAmerica.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coconut||10-29-2000||12:50 PM||||Cheveer2,<BR>Boy, am I catchin' your wave! Some great musicians you've got listed there. Although I'm pretty much open to most music, jazz is really taking a precedence in my musical preferences for the last couple of years and all due to the majority of artists that you previously mentioned.  Seattle has a great radio station at 98.9 on the dial. My next cd purchase is gonna be Panorama by Craig Chaqicuo (can't get enough of Cafe Carnival <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) not bad for an ex rocker with Jefferson Starship eh? The other thing that blows my mind is Obsession Confession by Slash (Guns and Roses) never thought he had it in him. If you can find it, Black Sand by Kalapana(local Hawaiian Band) has always been one of my favorite Cruisin' tunes, it's got both elements of hot and smooth to it.<P>Cruisin' On, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Oreif||10-29-2000||03:32 PM||||David Sanborn and a group called Passport.<BR>I like listening to the Jazz radio stations on my way home from work. Ususally switch between 2 of them. Helps calm the edge from the asylum I work at.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-29-2000||06:42 PM||||if you have a good public radio station nearby they usually play good stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever2||10-31-2000||11:32 AM||||Going to check out some of those artists mentioned above, as soon as I can.  Don't know why I never got any David Sanborn, already know from radio that I like him.<P>Philphine, you're absolutely right about NPR stations.  You must be catching WVXU out of Cincinnati.<P>And what was I thinking in my first list?!  Can't believe I failed to mention these:<P>Groups:  Fourplay, Acoustic Alchemy, Urban Knights (I only like their first album)<BR>Guitar:  Pat Metheny (yes!), Al DiMeola<BR>Sax:  Everette Harp<BR>Vocals:  Holly Cole<BR>Piano:  Vince Guaraldi (Charlie Brown music, what can I say?), Alex Bugnon, Bruce Hornsby (I don't care if he's crossover into Pop, more power to him, Cat can PLAY)<P>I also love Steely Dan and Sting.  And yes I do like many rock artists of a wide variety.<P>Others can join in besides Jazz lovers...  tell us who your favorites are!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||10-31-2000||12:53 PM||||I like(d) Frank Zappa. <BR>Little bit of jazz. <BR>Little bit of rock.<BR>A lot of humor, and a lot more insanity.<BR>He could play the most disjointed, improvisational piece of music you've ever heard. You'd swear he was making it up as he went along. But every time he played it, it would be identical. Note for note. Very talented musician and composer.<BR>I expect that this will probably draw some flames. Zappa was one *strange* individual.<BR>I've tried to listen to Steely Dan, with an open mind. It all sounds the same to me, though. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>"If I have to fake 'genuine concern' one more time today, I'm gonna scream!" -TCH||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||10-31-2000||02:30 PM||||Zappa was incredible.  I had the Apostrophe album until it's mysterious disappearance.  Guess somebody else liked it bad enough to steal for it.<P>If you like Zappa, maybe you like Jean-Luc Ponty.  His King Kong album was composed & arranged by Frank.  I'll send you the CD if you want it (free, don't worry about it).<P>You certainly don't have to like the same artists as I do.  There are about 6 billion opinions about music on this planet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||11-01-2000||02:08 AM||||cheever, louisville has 3 public radio stations that joined forces and don't over lap programing. that lets one station play all kinds of music, jazz included.||||reg||1
Z||000010||onfire||11-06-2000||01:21 PM||||Does anbody like the Blues? I work with this guy, and his music is pretty good. He sings at clubs,and has a few songs on the radio. Mainly just part time as he hasn't made it big yet. Anyway check out his website. <A HREF="http://www.frankjamesband.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.frankjamesband.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>"I know a little bit about everything, and alot about nothing"<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my little waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||MrPBody||11-08-2000||12:01 AM||||There's Jazz, and there's Jazz.  Dixieland and Ragtime are neglected forms.  Usually I don't think of Zappa as a Jazz man, but he fits.  Since I'm an Old F*rt, I really like Dave Brubeck.<BR>||||reg||1
